<% content_for :title, "Make your first cyberdeck" %>
<% content_for :body_class, "landing-page" %>
<% content_for :no_chrome, "1" %>

<%# The landing page. Built from Armand's Figma frames of 2026-09-17: a
    cutting mat background, tilted pixel serif headings in the program pink,
    irregular clipped panels, and one action. While sign-ups are closed the
    action is an RSVP email box. When they open it is "Get started", into /start. %>

<header class="hero" id="top"<%= " data-controller=\"utm\"".html_safe if utm_in_url? %>>
  <a class="badge" href="https://hackclub.com" aria-label="Hack Club">
    <%= image_tag "landing/hack-club-2026.svg", alt: "Hack Club 2026" %>
  </a>
  <% if signups_open? %>
    <%= link_to(signed_in? ? "Your setup" : "Log in", start_path, class: "btn btn-pink btn-login") %>
  <% end %>

  <%= image_tag "landing/display.png", alt: "", class: "prop prop-display" %>
  <%= image_tag "landing/pico.png",    alt: "", class: "prop prop-pico" %>

  <div class="hero-copy">
    <h1 class="title">
      <%= image_tag "landing/title.svg", alt: "Make your first cyberdeck", class: "title-img" %>
    </h1>
    <p class="tagline">And we’ll send you the parts to assemble it for free!</p>
    <p class="fineprint">
      A <a href="https://hackclub.com">Hack Club</a> program, by <a href="https://github.com/NanoMars">Armand</a>,
      free for teenagers worldwide.
    </p>
    <% if signups_open? %>
      <div class="actions">
        <%= link_to(@complete ? "Continue" : "Get started", start_path, class: "btn btn-pink btn-lg") %>
        <a class="btn btn-white btn-lg" href="#what">Learn more</a>
      </div>
    <% else %>
      <%# Sign-ups are closed for now, so the one action is an RSVP email box.
          Armand, 2026-09-21. SIGNUPS_OPEN=1 brings the buttons back. %>
      <%= render "landing/rsvp", slot: "top" %>
    <% end %>
  </div>

  <div class="scroll-hint" aria-hidden="true">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 80 40" width="80" height="40" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="6" stroke-linecap="square" aria-hidden="true">
      <path d="M6 6 40 34 74 6"/>
    </svg>
  </div>
</header>

<%# The jumper wires run from the hero down into the first fold, under the
    pink frame and under the panels, so they sit outside the hero. %>
<%= image_tag "landing/jumper-wires.png", alt: "", class: "prop prop-wires" %>

<main class="folds">

  <section class="fold fold-what" id="what">
    <h2 class="heading tilt">what is a cyberdeck?</h2>
    <div class="poly poly-pink halftone" style="--shape: polygon(7% 0, 97% 1%, 100% 22%, 91% 100%, 4% 96%, 0 78%); --dot-shift: 12%; --edge-r: 16px; --edge-b: 5px">
      <div class="poly-in">
        <p>A cyberdeck is a computer you make yourself.</p>
        <%# Armand's wording, 2026-09-21. Input before output. Armand. %>
        <p>Think of it as an app on your phone, but physical. It can be anything you want. For this program it has 3 requirements:</p>
        <ol>
          <li>It uses a Raspberry Pi Pico as its brain.</li>
          <li>It takes some kind of input, whether that is a button or a sensor.</li>
          <li>It has an output, whether that is a screen, a light or a sound.</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="fold fold-how" id="how">
    <h2 class="heading tilt">how it works</h2>
    <%# Armand's four step drawings of 2026-09-18, white lines on transparent. %>
    <ol class="cards">
      <li class="poly poly-pink card halftone" style="--shape: polygon(0 18px, 24px 0, 100% 0, 100% calc(100% - 26px), calc(100% - 20px) 100%, 0 100%); --tilt: -2deg; --dot-shift: 8%; --edge-r: 18px; --edge-b: 4px">
        <div class="poly-in">
          <p><span class="num">1.</span> Follow the guide to design and program your cyberdeck!</p>
          <%= image_tag "landing/how-1.png", alt: "Drawing of a raccoon coding on a laptop", class: "how-img", loading: "lazy" %>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="poly poly-pink card halftone" style="--shape: polygon(0 0, calc(100% - 26px) 0, 100% 24px, 100% 100%, 20px 100%, 0 calc(100% - 14px)); --tilt: 1.5deg; --dot-shift: 41%; --dot-flip: -1; --edge-r: 14px; --edge-b: 9px">
        <div class="poly-in">
          <p><span class="num">2.</span> Ship your project so other people can experience it!</p>
          <%= image_tag "landing/how-2.png", alt: "Drawing of a raccoon sailing a boat with a parcel aboard", class: "how-img", loading: "lazy" %>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="poly poly-pink card halftone" style="--shape: polygon(16px 0, calc(100% - 16px) 0, 100% 20px, 100% 100%, 0 100%, 0 28px); --tilt: -1deg; --dot-shift: 73%; --edge-r: 18px; --edge-b: 6px">
        <div class="poly-in">
          <p><span class="num">3.</span> We ship your parts to you!</p>
          <%= image_tag "landing/how-3.png", alt: "Drawing of a raccoon carrying a parcel", class: "how-img", loading: "lazy" %>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="poly poly-pink card halftone" style="--shape: polygon(0 0, 100% 0, 100% calc(100% - 30px), calc(100% - 24px) 100%, 18px 100%, 0 calc(100% - 12px)); --tilt: 2deg; --dot-shift: 22%; --dot-flip: -1; --edge-r: 13px; --edge-b: 7px">
        <div class="poly-in">
          <p><span class="num">4.</span> Assemble your cyberdeck!</p>
          <%= image_tag "landing/how-4.png", alt: "Drawing of a raccoon cheering beside a finished cyberdeck", class: "how-img", loading: "lazy" %>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="fold fold-parts" id="parts">
    <h2 class="heading tilt">What can I use?</h2>
    <ul class="parts">
      <% [
           ["Raspberry Pi Pico", "landing/pico.png",         "polygon(28px 0, 100% 0, 100% calc(100% - 22px), calc(100% - 14px) 100%, 0 100%, 0 30px)"],
           ["16×2 LCD display",  "landing/display.png",      "polygon(0 14px, 20px 0, calc(100% - 30px) 0, 100% 22px, 100% 100%, 0 100%)"],
           ["Jumper wires",      "landing/jumper-wires.png", "polygon(0 0, 100% 0, 100% calc(100% - 28px), calc(100% - 20px) 100%, 24px 100%, 0 calc(100% - 18px))"],
           ["Breadboard",        "landing/breadboard.png",                       "polygon(0 0, calc(100% - 30px) 0, 100% 16px, 100% calc(100% - 16px), calc(100% - 30px) 100%, 0 100%)"],
           ["Buttons",           "landing/buttons.png",                          "polygon(22px 0, 100% 0, 100% 100%, 26px 100%, 0 calc(100% - 20px), 0 24px)"],
           ["and more…",         :more,                      "polygon(0 10px, 18px 0, calc(100% - 18px) 0, 100% 16px, 100% calc(100% - 24px), calc(100% - 28px) 100%, 0 100%)"],
         ].each_with_index do |(name, img, shape), i| %>
        <li class="poly poly-pink part halftone<%= " part-more" if img == :more %>" style="--shape: <%= shape %>; --dot-shift: <%= (i * 37) % 100 %>%; --dot-flip: <%= i.odd? ? -1 : 1 %>; --edge-r: <%= [12, 9, 15, 10, 14, 11][i] %>px; --edge-b: <%= [5, 7, 4, 8, 5, 6][i] %>px">
          <div class="poly-in">
            <%# The last tile is "and more…", text only. Armand, 2026-09-18. %>
            <% if img && img != :more %>
              <%= image_tag img, alt: "", class: "part-img" %>
            <% end %>
            <strong><%= name %></strong>
          </div>
        </li>
      <% end %>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="fold fold-hc" id="hack-club">
    <div class="hc-row">
      <%# Social proof: photos from Hack Club events, three each side, tilted
          and overlapping like a pinboard. Alt text names the event kind. %>
      <ul class="snaps snaps-left" aria-label="Hack Club events">
        <li style="--r: -5deg"><%= image_tag "landing/hc/1.jpg", alt: "About 80 Hack Clubbers in front of a Midnight, case solved screen" %></li>
        <li style="--r: 3deg"><%= image_tag "landing/hc/2.jpg", alt: "Hack Clubbers at laptops around a long table" %></li>
        <li style="--r: -2deg"><%= image_tag "landing/hc/3.jpg", alt: "A bonfire on a beach at night" %></li>
      </ul>
      <div class="hc-center">
      <h2 class="heading tilt">what is hack club?</h2>
      <div class="poly poly-pink halftone" style="--shape: polygon(0 30px, 60px 0, 100% 0, 100% calc(100% - 50px), calc(100% - 90px) 100%, 40px 100%, 0 calc(100% - 40px)); --dot-shift: 55%; --edge-r: 20px; --edge-b: 6px">
        <div class="poly-in centered">
          <p><a href="https://hackclub.com">Hack Club</a> is a 501(c)(3) nonprofit that runs programs and events to encourage more students to build and publish engineering projects.</p>
          <p>We’re a community of 100,000+ high schoolers in 119 countries who learn by building things. Artists, engineers, hardware makers, game devs: everyone’s welcome, and nobody needs experience to start.</p>
          <p>Curious about Hack Club? Learn more about our <a href="https://hackclub.com/philosophy">philosophy</a>, <a href="https://hackclub.com/philanthropy">donors</a> or <a href="https://hackclub.com">other programs</a>.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      </div>
      <ul class="snaps snaps-right" aria-label="Hack Club events">
        <li style="--r: 4deg"><%= image_tag "landing/hc/4.jpg", alt: "Three Hack Clubbers looking at a phone together" %></li>
        <li style="--r: -3deg"><%= image_tag "landing/hc/5.jpg", alt: "A group photo on a hilltop" %></li>
        <li style="--r: 2deg"><%= image_tag "landing/hc/6.jpg", alt: "Two Hack Clubbers wiring a circuit next to a laptop" %></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="fold fold-faq" id="faq">
    <h2 class="heading tilt">FAQ</h2>
    <dl class="faq">
      <% [
           ["Am I eligible?",
            "Yes, if you are a teenager. Hack Club programs are for people aged 13 to 18, anywhere in the world.",
            "polygon(20px 0, 100% 0, 100% calc(100% - 20px), calc(100% - 28px) 100%, 0 100%, 0 26px)"],
           ["Is this legit?",
            "Yes. Hack Club is a 501(c)(3) nonprofit and has shipped hardware to teenagers through programs like this one for years. Ask anyone in the Hack Club Slack.",
            "polygon(0 0, calc(100% - 24px) 0, 100% 30px, 100% 100%, 30px 100%, 0 calc(100% - 28px))"],
           ["What can I make?",
            "Anything with a Raspberry Pi Pico for a brain and at least one input. A tiny handheld, a desk gadget, a sensor station, a game console. You decide.",
            "polygon(0 16px, 30px 0, calc(100% - 20px) 0, 100% 10px, 100% 100%, 0 100%)"],
           ["What if I’ve never done electronics before?",
            "Then you are exactly who this is for. The guide starts from zero, and you write and run your code in a simulator in the browser before any parts arrive.",
            "polygon(16px 0, 100% 0, 100% calc(100% - 26px), calc(100% - 30px) 100%, 14px 100%, 0 calc(100% - 18px), 0 12px)"],
         ].each_with_index do |(q, a, shape), i| %>
        <div class="poly poly-pink faq-item halftone" style="--shape: <%= shape %>; --dot-shift: <%= (i * 29 + 60) % 100 %>%; --dot-flip: <%= i.odd? ? 1 : -1 %>; --edge-r: <%= [14, 10, 18, 12][i] %>px; --edge-b: <%= [5, 8, 4, 7][i] %>px">
          <div class="poly-in">
            <dt><%= q %></dt>
            <dd><%= a %></dd>
          </div>
        </div>
      <% end %>
    </dl>
    <div class="cta-end" id="rsvp-end">
      <% if signups_open? %>
        <%= link_to(@complete ? "Continue" : "Get started", start_path, class: "btn btn-pink btn-lg") %>
      <% else %>
        <%= render "landing/rsvp", slot: "rsvp-end" %>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </section>

  <%# The Hack Club handbook's Promise Policy: every YSWS website links the
      privacy policy and terms, and the fulfillment bounty, in the footer.
      The Gap Year's name sits above the fold in the hero fine print.
      Three lowercase words, as on jamegam's footer. Armand, 2026-09-21. %>
  <footer class="foot">
    <p>A <a href="https://hackclub.com">Hack Club</a> program, run by <a href="https://github.com/NanoMars">Armand</a>.</p>
    <p class="foot-links">
      <a href="https://hackclub.com/privacy-and-terms">privacy policy</a>
      <a href="https://forms.hackclub.com/bounty">fulfillment</a>
      <a href="https://hackclub.com">hack club</a>
    </p>
  </footer>
</main>
